# Line endings for files that are consumed by Linux tooling.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with git's autocrlf behaviour, so
# text files are checked out with CRLF. That is harmless for TypeScript and
# for documentation, but not for anything a Linux shell or a container build
# reads: a trailing \r inside a `run: |` block in a GitHub Actions workflow
# becomes part of the command and fails with errors like
# `$'\r': command not found`, and a CRLF shell script fails the same way.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto`: that would renormalise the entire
# existing history-worth of files in one commit and bury real changes. Only
# the files that actually break are pinned.

# Container build inputs.
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile        text eol=lf
.dockerignore       text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml  text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml text eol=lf

# nginx configuration, read inside the container.
*.conf              text eol=lf

# CI workflows — these contain shell.
/.github/**/*.yml   text eol=lf
/.github/**/*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Any shell script, wherever it lives.
*.sh                text eol=lf
